From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SeungJun Lee <mps756@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:21:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] FSA: Validate OPFS transfer tokens by StorageKey

OPFS handles are partitioned by StorageKey. Comparing only the origin
when redeeming a transfer token lets a same-origin context in another
top-level site redeem a handle for the wrong partition.

Validate the token URL's StorageKey for sandboxed OPFS handles while
preserving origin-scoped redemption for native file system handles.

Bug: 508285208
Change-Id: I5bec88398138fe5cdd2a0520b93c1e377fb8588e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8471067
Reviewed-by: Rahul Singh <rahsin@microsoft.com>
Reviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: SeungJun Lee <mps756@gmail.com>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1707872}
(cherry picked from commit 625dedb4a0787aebaad22b6397ea9398252cbe58)

[FlyWeb] Also passes the full StorageKey again in
DidResolveForSerializeHandle() (undoes the origin-only call of 0030), as
upstream 71ea1e9367 does on top of this change.
